##DESCRIPTION
##  Algebra problem: linear inequality
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## tcao , PAID on 11-24-2003

## DBsubject(Algebra)
## DBchapter(Absolute value expressions and functions)
## DBsection(Absolute value inequalities)
## Date(6/3/2002)
## MLT(algIneq)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('Precalculus')
## AuthorText1('Stewart, Redlin, Watson')
## EditionText1('3')
## Section1('1.7')
## Problem1('11')
## KEYWORDS('algebra', 'linear inequality')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a    = random(1, 20);
$b    = random(1, 20);
$left = 2 * ($a + $b);
Context('Interval');
$int = Compute("[$left,inf)");

BEGIN_PGML
The solution of the linear inequality
[``` \frac{1}{2}x -[$a] > [$b] ```]
is [_]{$int}

*Write the answer in interval notation.*

[@ helpLink('intervals'); @]*

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[```
\begin{aligned}
\frac{1}{2} x - [$a] & > [$b] \\
\frac{1}{2} x & > [$b]+[$a] = [$b+$a] \\
x &>  2([$b+$a]) = [$left]
\end{aligned}```]

So the interval is [``[$int]``].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
